5. Project Design and Working Methods
	5.1 SMART Project Goal
Within 4 weeks i will develop a notepad application that encrypts the contents on save and decrypts them if a key is provided.
	- Specific: Build a notepad application that encrypts your information on save.
	- Measurable: Application should be able to save and reopen encrypted files without data loss or corruption.
	- Achieveable: The project is realistic for a beginner using Python.
	- Realistic/Relevant: Learning encryption and file handling is achievable within four weeks and directly contributes to my IT skills.
	- Time-Based: Completed within a four week timeframe.
	5.2 Agile Methodology
	The project follows Agile metodology to ensure flexibility and continuous improvement.

	Sprint Planning
	- Sprint 1 (Week 1): Complete analysis, define criteria and research about encryption methods.
	- Sprint 2 (Week 2): Create design document, decide what encryption will be used and ask for feedback.
	- Sprint 3 (Week 3): Develop realisation document, design the UI and write the algorithms for encryption, and decryption.
	- Sprint 4 (Week 4): Perform testing, put the evidence in portfolio and ask for feedback.
	Agile Practices
	- Daily self-checks: Track progress against functional requirements.
	- Sprint Reviews: Demo prototype to peers, teachers or self-test.
	- Retrospectives: Reflect on coding challenges and workflow efficiency.
	User Stories
	- As a user, I want my information to be safe.
	- As a user, I want my information to be available for reading and redacting only by authorized people.
	- As a user, I want an intuitive interface.
	- As a developer, I want secure encryption algorithms.
